{
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "text": "What can a boolean hold?",
      "options": [
        "Only True or False",
        "True or False, and any text as well",
        "Any number from 0 to 1",
        "Any text in quotes"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "text": "Which line makes a boolean variable?",
      "options": [
        "is_online = true",
        "is_online = \"True\"",
        "is_online = True",
        "is_online == True"
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "text": "What happens when this runs?",
      "code": "has_key = false\nprint(has_key)",
      "options": [
        "It stops with an error: it has to be written False",
        "It prints false",
        "It prints False",
        "It prints nothing"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "text": "What does this print?",
      "code": "age = 20\nprint(age < 18)",
      "options": ["True", "False", "age < 18", "20"],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q5",
      "text": "What is a condition like `x == 5` really?",
      "options": [
        "A number",
        "A piece of text",
        "A line that puts 5 in x",
        "A boolean: it is True or False"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q6",
      "text": "When is `left and right` True?",
      "options": [
        "When at least one of them is True",
        "Only when both are True",
        "When both are False",
        "When left is True, whatever right is"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q7",
      "text": "When is `left or right` True?",
      "options": [
        "Only when both are True",
        "Only when exactly one of them is True",
        "When at least one of them is True",
        "Only when left is True"
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q8",
      "text": "What is `not True`?",
      "options": ["False", "True", "An error: not needs a variable", "Nothing"],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q9",
      "text": "What is `True and False`?",
      "options": ["True", "True and False", "An error", "False"],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q10",
      "text": "What is `False or True`?",
      "options": ["False", "True", "False or True", "An error"],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q11",
      "text": "What is `False and False`?",
      "options": ["True: two False make a True", "An error", "False", "Nothing"],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q12",
      "text": "In the lesson, `age = 20` and `has_license = False`. What runs for `if age >= 18 and has_license == True:`?",
      "options": [
        "The else: True and False is False",
        "The if: age >= 18 is True",
        "Both the if and the else",
        "Nothing: Python stops with an error"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q13",
      "text": "Does `if has_license:` mean the same as `if has_license == True:`?",
      "options": [
        "No: the first one is always True",
        "No: the first one stops with an error",
        "Only inside a while",
        "Yes: has_license is already a boolean"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q14",
      "text": "In the lesson's club, `is_vip = False` and `has_invitation = True`. What does `if is_vip or has_invitation:` lead to?",
      "options": [
        "Access denied",
        "Welcome to the club",
        "Welcome to the club, then Access denied",
        "An error, since is_vip is False"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q15",
      "text": "What does `not` do to a boolean?",
      "options": [
        "It flips it: True becomes False and False becomes True",
        "It makes it False, whatever it was",
        "It deletes the variable",
        "It checks that the variable exists"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q16",
      "text": "`is_logged_in` is False. Does `if not is_logged_in:` run its block?",
      "options": [
        "No: is_logged_in is False",
        "No: not works only on True",
        "Yes: not False is True",
        "It stops with an error"
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q17",
      "text": "What do we call a boolean variable that keeps a loop going, like `running`?",
      "options": ["A counter", "A range", "A comment", "A flag"],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q18",
      "text": "`running` becomes False in the middle of a `while running:` loop. When does the loop stop?",
      "options": [
        "At its next check: the rest of that iteration still runs",
        "Right away, in the middle of the iteration",
        "After one more full iteration",
        "Never: a while loop needs break"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q19",
      "text": "What does the lesson's flag loop print?",
      "code": "running = True\nnumber = 0\nwhile running:\n    print(number)\n    number = number + 1\n    if number == 3:\n        running = False\nprint(\"Done\")",
      "options": ["0\n1\n2\n3\nDone", "0\n1\n2\nDone", "1\n2\n3\nDone", "0\n1\n2"],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q20",
      "text": "Why does the lesson call a flag a clean alternative to break?",
      "options": [
        "A flag makes the loop run faster",
        "break doesn't work in a while loop",
        "The loop's own condition closes it, instead of jumping out abruptly",
        "A flag stops the loop in the middle of the iteration"
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q21",
      "text": "What does `print(5 == 5)` print?",
      "options": ["5 == 5", "5", "10", "True"],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q22",
      "text": "What is the difference between `=` and `==`?",
      "options": [
        "= puts a value in a variable; == compares two values and gives True or False",
        "None, they mean the same",
        "== puts a value in a variable; = compares",
        "= is for numbers, == is for text"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q23",
      "text": "What does this print?",
      "code": "x = 7\nprint(x != 7)",
      "options": ["True", "False", "7", "x != 7"],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q24",
      "text": "In the Command Console mission, the user types status, then hello, then shutdown. What does the program print?",
      "options": [
        "System active\nUnknown command",
        "System active\nUnknown command\nUnknown command\nClosing console...",
        "System active\nUnknown command\nClosing console...",
        "Closing console..."
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q25",
      "text": "In the Command Console mission, what happens once the user types shutdown?",
      "options": [
        "The program stops at once, without printing Closing console...",
        "It prints Unknown command and asks again",
        "powered_on becomes False, but the loop keeps asking for commands",
        "powered_on becomes False, the loop stops at its next check and Closing console... is printed"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q26",
      "text": "In the Command Console mission, why does `powered_on` start as True?",
      "options": [
        "So the while loop runs and asks for the first command",
        "So the program prints True first",
        "Every variable has to start as True",
        "So shutdown is typed by itself"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q27",
      "text": "After `age = 15` and `is_adult = age >= 18`, what does `is_adult` hold?",
      "options": ["True", "False", "15", "The text age >= 18"],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q28",
      "text": "Which condition is True when age is 20 and has_license is True, and False as soon as one of them fails?",
      "options": [
        "age >= 18 or has_license",
        "age >= 18 and not has_license",
        "age >= 18 and has_license",
        "not has_license"
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q29",
      "text": "Why does a `while True:` loop with no break never stop?",
      "options": [
        "True means the loop has to stop, but Python ignores it",
        "It stops after the first iteration",
        "It stops once it prints True",
        "Its condition is always True"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q30",
      "text": "What is `not False`?",
      "options": ["False", "True", "An error: not needs a variable", "Nothing"],
      "answer": 1
    }
